  "description": "An Armenian mountain year unfolds as pure rhythm. Shepherds swept downriver clutching sheep, hay sleds flying downhill, a wedding, a flock pouring over a ridge — Pelechian's \"distance montage\" builds meaning between shots that never touch. Thirty minutes, no dialogue, elemental.\n\nFilm-essay about shepherds living in the Armenian highlands, about the contradiction and the harmony between man and nature.",
